F. Exact identities and mechanisms
  I1 c3(T)=C(n,3)-sum_v C(d+(v),2); global triangle count adds no score data.
  I2 rooted triangle row v=(C(d,2), d(n-1-d)-c_v, C(n-1-d,2), c_v).
  I3 for each induced k-type vector p and vertex v: A_v + D_v = p,
     sum_v A_v=k p, sum_v D_v=(n-k)p (A=containing incidence, D=deleted profile).
  I4 over Q, rowspace(A)=rowspace(D), hence ranks agree exactly for 0<k<n.
     Over F2 ranks differ by at most one; if n even and k odd they agree.
  I5 the full deck determines every proper induced-type profile by Kelly double counting.
     It also determines paired (card,c3-loss), so c3-loss is not a genuine boundary repair.
  I6 card + missing-vertex outdegree is a genuine marked-boundary coordinate; it resolves
     every isomorphism collision checked through n=6, while deck + unpaired scores does not.
  I7 every four-card is classified by (q,h): q=#cyclic triangle faces in {0,1,2},
     h=#universal sources-#universal sinks in {-1,0,1}.  With D=sum_v[
     C(d+(v),3)-C(d-(v),3)] and C4=#q=2 cards,
     N_plus=((n-3)C3-2C4+D)/2 and N_minus=((n-3)C3-2C4-D)/2,
     and N0=C(n,4)-(n-3)C3+C4.  Thus chirality is variable but score-determined;
     the directed Hamiltonian C4 count is the only new scalar in the four-profile.
  I8 complementing W_{r,r+1} gives KG(2r+1,r), and the displayed intersection-kernel
     is its exact rational inverse.  The check is exhaustive over all intersection classes
     for r=1..6; the checked finite F2 ranks equal C(2r,r).
  I9 the unmarked maximal proper-flag type-sequence distribution is exactly deck-equivalent:
     partition flags by their omitted last vertex to derive it from the full deck; conversely
     the terminal (n-1)-type in each sequence recovers every card multiplicity.  Therefore
     unmarked flag gluing cannot repair a deck collision; a boundary/card mark is essential.
  I10 exhaustive local-rule optimization gives 144/1024=4608/32768=9/64 for d=4,5.
      At d=5 the 4608 successful edge tournaments are exactly one switching/relabel orbit
      with seed 10 and stabilizer order 5; this is finite-exact, not a literature-priority claim.
  I11 rule 1415 is not an opaque table: on every labelled five-tournament its sign is
      one quarter of an alternating sum of five triangle-flux Pfaffians minus full edge parity.
      Its exact Fourier support is 15 degree-six bowties plus the degree-ten parity monomial.
  I12 the d=5 rule is the unique alternating apex lift of d=4 rule 8 in the checked convention:
